.TH SIGFPE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
sigfpe \- Raise a SIGFPE signal

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/sig.h>

.IB int
.IB sigfpe(void);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBsigfpe\fR function is used to raise a SIGFPE signal.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The \fBsigfpe\fR function returns 0 on success, and -1 on failure.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBsigfpe\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/sig.h>

int main() {
    printf("Raising SIGFPE signal...\n");

    int r = sigfpe();

    if(r == 0)
        printf("SIGFPE signal raised successfully.\n");
    else
        printf("Failed to raise SIGFPE signal.\n");

    return 0;
}
.nef